WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.770
In 2019, 99 per cent of the world's population
lived where WHO air quality guideline

2
00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.230
levels were not met.

3
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.770
Outdoor air pollution caused an estimated
4.2 million premature deaths that year.

4
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:20.130
In 2021, a London coroner's report named
air pollution exposure as a cause of

5
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.390
a 9-year-old girl's death.

6
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.670
So does everyone in a
city breathe the same air?

7
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.390
Or only people near factories?

8
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.550
Or in the suburbs?

9
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.450
In this mission, you'll
explain the urban heat island,

10
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.510
and why it grows stronger after sunset.

11
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.810
Then you'll map air
pollution inside London,

12
00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:41.370
and evaluate how the city
is trying to clean it up.

13
00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:45.400
Your mission: find out who
breathes a city's dirtiest air.
